body:
Manuscript construction checkpoint: built the complete reader-facing H1-H4 skeleton in MANUSCRIPT_DRAFT.md v0.2, then challenged it before prose.

Challenge artifact: audits/MANUSCRIPT_HEADING_SKELETON_CHALLENGE_2026-09-23.md.

Findings:
- all C1-C5 now have manuscript owners;
- H[F] corpus admission has an explicit owner in 2.3;
- package TRACE and COMPOSE remain separately owned;
- H_R receives intentionally asymmetric space because it is result-sensitive;
- two compression OPENs remain: whether PROFILE keeps a separate 4.1 after prose, and whether 7.4 survives whole-draft compression;
- interface controls added conceptually for 3.4.4->4, 4.5.3->6.1, and 6.4->7.4;
- three exploratory PD probes found a convergent missing reviewer-facing object: the manuscript lacked a visible answer to "Are you deciding which Genesis 1:1 reading is actually correct?"

Strict-gain fix implemented:
2.2.4 "A Second-Order Analysis Without a First-Order Verdict."

A16-style regression: no protected regression. Skeleton accepted as DRAFTING_BASELINE.

Next action: begin prose at Section 2.1. No further global architecture cycle before prose unless drafting exposes a load-bearing defect.
